%description:

TcpCubic.tcpFriendliness:on -- the window never grows slower than the Reno-friendly estimate.

The claim (TcpCubic.ned): "never grow slower than the Reno-friendly estimate of RFC 9438 section
4.3, which grows by about 0.53 segments per RTT (alpha_cubic for beta = 0.7); false: no
estimate".

The classes: on (true, the default) and off (false). The code: with the estimate, the window
grows at least as fast as the Reno-friendly estimate (TcpCubic::update()); without it, it
follows the cubic curve, which stays below W_max until K. This test separates "on" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, with TcpCubic and without SACK, which sends 5000000 bytes to host2,
whose window is 1000000 bytes; the round trip is 40 ms, and the tap drops the 15th data
segment once. K is about 3 s. Observation: level 3, at 2.6 s, about 2.2 s after the loss,
the window is more than 8 segments above W_max: the Reno-friendly estimate.

%# parameter: TcpCubic.tcpFriendliness
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.tcpFriendliness
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpCubicTcpFriendlinessOn")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 15th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(2.6)
                 .describe("the window at 2.6 s")
                 .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "state.snd_cwnd > (state.cubic_last_max_cwnd + 8) * 1448"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpCubicTcpFriendlinessOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.tcpFriendliness = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpCubic"
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.tcp.sackSupport = false
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 1000000
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 5000000B
sim-time-limit = 4s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpCubicTcpFriendlinessOn: PASS
